      "methodology": "Identical FineWeb byte crops, batch 8 x 2,048 bytes, Muon/AdamW parameter split, WSD schedule, bf16 autocast, compiled training, 4,000 updates = 65.536M training bytes, fixed validation crops every 400 steps, one RTX 3090. The primary Braid/MHA comparison uses three paired seeds (1337/2027/4242); one-seed arms are mechanism screens, not rankings.",
      "caveats": [
        "Equal-byte quality still favours the dense MHA Transformer by 0.019 bits/byte. Braid's advantage is systems cost, not loss.",
        "Steady-state throughput excludes the first logged interval so sequential torch.compile cache population cannot flatter later arms; wall time and energy deliberately include compilation.",
        "Energy is whole-card draw from process start to checkpoint save, not isolated kernel energy.",
        "Analytical FLOPs omit norms, embeddings, elementwise work and the exact suffix-table operations; measured time and energy include them.",
        "These are ~30M-parameter runs. They do not license any claim about the 300M model."
      ]
    },
